<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coventry Carol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century; text dated 14 March <a href="/years/1534">1534</a>, music dated 13 May <a href="/years/1591">1591</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The &quot;Coventry Carol&quot; is the second of three songs in the Pageant of the Shearmen and Tailors, a nativity play that was one of the Coventry Mystery Plays, performed by the city's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guilds</a>. The pageant tells the Christmas story from the second chapter of the Gospel of Matthew.</p></div>
